    {
      "id": 10,
      "title": "Worker liveness (opt-in actual pass observer)",
      "type": "text",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 34,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 4
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "Opt in with `gregale_event_recovery_worker=\"true\"` only when this target exports the monitored Go or Node recovery-pass cache. Health polling and HTTP scrapes never refresh worker activity. The first/next pass must start within the idle bound; an active pass must return within its duration expectation. These are alerts, not deadlines or automatic recovery. Outcomes are latest joined-pass gauges, not totals/rates, and may belong to the previous pass while another is active. A completed or empty pass does not prove callback/business success or global drain. Missing evidence is Unknown. [Worker runbook](https://github.com/poyrazK/faas/blob/main/docs/runbooks/GregaleEventRecovery.md#worker-liveness). Node pool-cleanup failures and typed cleanup uncertainty can overlap known settlement outcomes; never sum all outcome fields."
      }
    },
